# Data files that live inside the packages and are read at run time.
#
# A wheel built from this tree carried none of them (outside audit of 27 November 2026): the page the UI server
# sends was missing, so an installed copy could not serve it. setuptools puts a file named here into the wheel when
# it lies inside a package, because include-package-data is on by default. The package-data table of pyproject.toml
# would be the usual place; that file is frozen by a preregistration, so it is done here.
#
# Not solved by this file: the specifications under specifications/ lie outside every package, so an installed
# wheel still cannot load apedp_dyn.conf.discovery_checks. Use a checkout (pip install -e .) until that is decided.
include apedp_dyn/ui/dashboard.html
include apedp_dyn/sandbox/APEDPX_FROZEN_v1_18.json
include LICENSE
